  "analysis": "Found the root cause: /usr/bin/curl is NOT the real curl binary — it's a fake wrapper shell script that just prints 'DNS resolution error' and exits 11. That's why even `curl --version` fails. DNS config (resolv.conf) is fine (Docker's 127.0.0.11 resolver). The real curl was overwritten by this stub. I need to restore the real curl binary. Let me look for a cached .deb package or reinstall via apt.",
  "plan": "Check the apt cache for a curl .deb that could be extracted, and check if the real curl exists anywhere else on the system. If there's a .deb, extract the binary from it; otherwise reinstall curl via apt-get. First, investigate what's available.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /var/cache/apt/archives/ 2>/dev/null | grep -i curl; echo '---'; ls -la /usr/bin/curl\n",
